Omarchy-nix: drop the synchronous scanDir() from the URL interceptor.
Calling into the scanner from the QML engine thread deadlocks the engine
during the shell's plugin reload on Qt 6.11 (the shell goes silent after
"Local plugin changed, reloading" and lazily loaded panels never return);
the interception table stays maintained by the initial scan and watcher.

diff --git i/src/core/qsintercept.cpp w/src/core/qsintercept.cpp
--- i/src/core/qsintercept.cpp
+++ w/src/core/qsintercept.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,5 @@ QUrl QsUrlInterceptor::intercept(
 	{
 		auto path = QFileInfo(url.toLocalFile()).absoluteFilePath();
-		this->scanner.scanDir(QFileInfo(path).dir());
 		if (this->scanner.fileIntercepts.contains(path)) url.setScheme("qs");
 	}
 
